1. Ownership

The GTG's Backrooms mod (the "Software") is the work and exclusive property of GTGpuke (the
"Author"). This includes its source code and compiled code, its tests, its textures, models, translations and data,
and its documentation. The Software is protected by French intellectual property law and by international copyright
treaties.

The Software is not free or open-source software. Even when published publicly, it is not licensed to anyone, except
as Section 2 permits.

2. What is permitted

Without any other agreement, anyone may only:
a) install and use, unmodified, a JAR file of the Software published by the Author, to play, in single player or on
   a server;
b) read the source code where the Author publishes it;
c) exercise, on a public repository, what the GitHub Terms of Service grant its users: viewing it and forking it on
   GitHub. This grants no other right.

3. What is forbidden

Without the Author's prior written permission, it is forbidden, for all or part of the Software:
a) to copy or reproduce it, except as required by the use permitted in Section 2;
b) to modify, adapt or translate it, or to create derivative works. This includes reusing code, textures or other
   assets in another project;
c) to distribute, republish, host, sell, rent, lend or sublicense it, including in a modpack, on a mod platform or on
   a mirror site;
d) to use it to build a dataset or to train an artificial intelligence model;
e) to remove or alter this notice or any proprietary notice.

This license does not restrict the rights that the law grants to the lawful user of a software program and that
cannot be waived (Article L. 122-6-1 of the French Intellectual Property Code).

4. Permissions

Requests for permission go to the Author, through the Author's GitHub account (https://github.com/GTGpuke).

A permission exists only if it is in writing. It is personal and cannot be transferred.

5. Termination

Any breach of this license ends the right to use the Software. This termination is immediate and requires no notice.

6. No warranty

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the extent permitted by law, the Author is not
liable for any damage arising from its use, including the loss or corruption of worlds or saves.

7. Third-party components

This license covers only the Author's work. Minecraft belongs to Mojang and Microsoft. Fabric Loader and Fabric API
remain under their own licenses; the Software depends on them but does not bundle them.

NOT AN OFFICIAL MINECRAFT PRODUCT. NOT APPROVED BY OR ASSOCIATED WITH MOJANG OR MICROSOFT.

